# Tougather — environment.
#
# Every one of these is optional. The app runs with none of them set: it stores
# work in the browser, the AI is a local stub that says so, live sessions run
# through the built-in relay, and checkout walks the whole flow without
# charging. Setting a group switches that group on; nothing else changes.
#
# Anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is compiled into the browser bundle and is
# public. Everything else stays on the server. Nothing in this file belongs in
# git — copy it to .env.local, and set the same names in your host's dashboard.

# ── The site ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where this is deployed. Used to resolve link previews and canonical URLs;
# without it they point at tougather.com, which is right in production and
# wrong on a preview deploy.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://tougather.com

# ── AI (OpenRouter) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One key, many models. Without it the assistant is the local stub, which is a
# working product rather than a broken one — it just can't reason.
#
# Server-side only, on purpose: the browser posts to /api/ai and the key never
# leaves the server. A NEXT_PUBLIC_ variant of this would be a leaked key.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Rotation, in preference order. A request walks the list until one model
# answers; a model that fails is demoted for a minute so the next request
# doesn't pay the same timeout. Leave unset for the built-in list, which ends
# in openrouter/auto so a retired slug can never leave you without a model.
# OPENROUTER_MODELS=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5,openai/gpt-4.1,google/gemini-2.5-flash,openrouter/auto

# Your deployed URL. OpenRouter uses it for attribution in their dashboard;
# without it requests still work, they're just anonymous.
# OPENROUTER_APP_URL=https://tougather.com

# Point at any OpenAI-compatible gateway instead of OpenRouter. Leave unset
# unless you're self-hosting one — it exists so the rotation can be tested
# against a stub, and so a fork isn't needed to change hosts.
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# ── Database, accounts and live sessions (Supabase) ───────────────────────
# Run supabase/schema.sql against the project first, and turn on anonymous
# sign-ins — that is what lets the free plan keep work without a login.
#
# These also switch live collaboration over to Supabase Realtime. That matters
# on any host that autoscales: the built-in relay keeps its rooms in memory, so
# two people served by different instances would never meet.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Server-side only. Never expose this: it bypasses row level security.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── Payments (Stripe) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Also fill in STRIPE_PRICE_IDS in src/lib/billing/index.ts, or checkout will
# answer 501 with "no price id set" rather than charging the wrong thing.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
